# ==============================================================================
# GitHub Issue Generator - Configuration Example (.env.example)
# Copy this file to .env or docs/.env.
# WARNING: .env contains sensitive credentials and must NEVER be committed to Git.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. GITHUB_REPOSITORY (Optional)
# Target GitHub repository in "owner/repo" format (e.g. facebook/react, hsiong/project-skills).
#
# Purpose and Resolution:
# - Used to construct GitHub REST API endpoint: POST https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues
# - Default behavior: Optional. If omitted or empty, the script automatically parses
#   `git config --get remote.origin.url` from your local git repository.
#
# When to configure explicitly:
#   1. Submitting issues across repositories (e.g. from a personal fork to upstream official repository).
#   2. Local origin points to internal GitLab/Gitee, but issues are tracked on GitHub.
#   3. Offline directories or workspaces without a configured git remote.
#   4. Convenience: avoids passing owner/repo via CLI arguments each time.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_REPOSITORY=owner/repo

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. GITHUB_TOKEN (Required credential)
# GitHub Personal Access Token with repository issue write permissions (issues:write or repo scope).
#
# Notes:
# - If GITHUB_TOKEN or GH_TOKEN is already exported in your shell environment,
#   you do not need to configure it here.
# - If not set in the environment, the script reads it from this file.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token
